Subject: [PATCH] avutil/aarch64: add NEON NAL start-code search

Upstream proposal: https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/21475
Patchwork snapshot: https://patchwork.ffmpeg.org/project/ffmpeg/patch/57934/
Adapted to FFmpeg master e0e6ca1e29ef3f6b1e9b7d8656fe341eee8cf647.

Move the shared muxer search into avutil and dispatch once to NEON where
compiled and supported. Install the public header; retain muxer callers.
Fix upstream search-start underreads, final complete start-code handling,
and vector-boundary false negatives. Return the exclusive end on misses,
require no padding, and keep both scalar and assembly loads in range.
Use a conservative any-zero NEON candidate filter so zero pairs crossing
vectors and blocks reach the existing detailed scan.

